From u8aa9b8cc06fdc99c at groups.google.com  Thu Jan 14 01:01:19 2016
From: u8aa9b8cc06fdc99c at groups.google.com (Bob Carpenter)
Date: Thu, 14 Jan 2016 01:01:19 +0000
Subject: Re: [stan-users] Simple understanding of STAN syntax
Message-ID: <CG3xM1TCacs.oue0is83AQAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <CG3xM1TCacs.1CIv8cI1AQAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
References: <CG3xM1TCacs.nmjTxZwuAQAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com> <CG3xM1TCacs.1CIv8cI1AQAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-users/c/CG3xM1TCacs/m/oue0is83AQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

(N x K) x (K x 1) = (N x 1)

matrix x vector = vector

Stan reduces types where possible --- the index to
the manual lists all the rules.

It needs to be of size N because it's parallel
to y!

- Bob

