One real example I've been hit with is when I need to re-construct a matrix inside of the ODE, since I can't pass it matrix data types :(

On Tuesday, January 12, 2016 at 11:42:19 AM UTC-8, Bob Carpenter wrote:
> Can you show us a real example.  For the toy example you gave, the
> right approach would be to declare the variable with the shape you
> want to begin with.
>
> And it's "<-" not "=" for assignment in Stan.
>
> - Bob
>
> > On Jan 12, 2016, at 7:44 AM, Nikolay Evdokimov <kolyaev...@gmail.com> wrote:
