Subject: #include "functions.txt" not working in rstan
Message-ID: <mAB8cldvTWw.PktLwKSTAAAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-users/c/mAB8cldvTWw/m/PktLwKSTAAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I've been trying to use rstan's pre-processor #include ability to share common functions among a variety of models, but the model isn't recognizing the functions when I run it in R.

A simple example:

toy_fun.stan:
 // sqrt of a vector (elementwise)
  vector sqrt_vec(vector x) {
    vector[dims(x)[1]] res;

    for (m in 1:dims(x)[1]){
        res[m] <- sqrt(x[m]);
    }
    return res;
  }
// other functions...

toy.stan:
functions{
  #include "toy_fun.stan"
}
data{
  int n;
  vector[n] x;
}
transformed data{
  vector[n] sX;
  sX <- sqrt_vec(x);
}
// The rest of the model follows

These files are included in the same directory, which is also R's working directory.  Upon running the model:

library(rstan)
setwd("~/R/ToyExample")

n <- 100
x <- rnorm(n, 1, 2)^2

toyFit <- stan("toy.stan", iter = 400)

I receive the following error message:
SYNTAX ERROR, MESSAGE(S) FROM PARSER:

No matches for:

  sqrt_vec(vector)

Function sqrt_vec not found.

ERROR at line 10

  8:    transformed data{
  9:      vector[n] sX;
 10:      sX <- sqrt_vec(x);
                           ^
 11:    }

Error in stanc(file = file, model_code = model_code, model_name = model_name,  :
  failed to parse Stan model 'toy' due to the above error.

I have also tried a few variations in the #include statement, such as using the full path; none have worked.

Is there something I'm missing?  I'd really like to be able to use this feature. I'm using rstan 2.9.0 on linux, and the same system had no difficulties compiling the rstanarm models.

