brms allows to do this including setting appropriate bounds on the parameters to avoid divergent transitions. However, I write the following in the documentation of this feature: "... In most situations, it is not useful to restrict fixed effects parameters through bounded priors, but if you really want to this is the way to go."
After reading your comments, I may replace "not useful" with something stronger, though ;-)

